  "Description": "Complete change of approach now that I know to set the maximum Pitch and Roll to 180 degrees. Also set the output pitch to the measured (from the SimHub manual control window) angles the H3R is capable of.\r\n\r\nV2.1 - Increases the amount of movement  on pitch and roll - make things a bit more aggressive.\r\nChange traction loss algorithm to lateral velocity.\r\n\r\nV2.2 \r\nIncrease DOF H3 movement on roll.  Increasing Motion Scaling->Motion Range from 18->25 for Roll and Roll Rate.  The roll effect  was feeling a little anemic.\r\n\r\nV2.3\r\nExported the file using SimHub V9.9.11 to upgrade to the latest lua file format.\r\nPitch Effect \r\n- Change MaxInputRange from 180 to 90 - you can't go outside the range -90 to 90 (duh!). \r\n- Change MaxOutputRange from 24 to 25 to match Pitch Rate effect.\r\nPitch Rate Effect\r\n- Both Motion Scaling output ranges set to 17.\r\nSurge to Pitch Effect\r\n- Increase Acceleration Input Limit (MaxInputRangeNegative) from 10 to 40 m/s.  Change output value from 9.5 to 17.\r\n- Increase Deceleration Input Limit (MaxInputRangePositive) from 25 to 45 m/s.  Change output value from 9.5 to 17.\r\n\r\nV2.4\r\nSurge to Pitch Effect\r\n- Decrease Acceleration Input Limit from 40 to 6 to get some feeling when punching the throttle.\r\n\r\nV2.5\r\nPitch Effect\r\n- turn off for now because it causes bumps in the pitch direction when pulling and pushing on the stick.  When you do a steep dive this effect will point your motion rig down (or up) and hold it until you pull out.  Ultimately I decided that effect wasn't worth the distracting bumps when changing pitch inputs.\r\n\r\nSurge to Pitch Effect\r\n- Increase Motion scaling/ output from 17 to 20 to provide more feeling of acceleration.\r\n- Set smoothing to 90% to remove some bumpy behavior when advancing or retarding the throttle.  There is a trade off here - smoothing removes the distracting bumps but also adds lag especially for the higher values.  At 99% the acceleration feeling was very smooth with no bumpy feelings but it would add 5-10 seconds before the H3 fully leaned back for the full feeling of acceleration.\r\n\r\nV2.6\r\nRoll Effect\r\n- Disable Washout filter, I think I enabled it by accident,.\r\n\r\nSway to Roll Effect (S2R)\r\n- Turn effect off but it still gets used when landing/taxiing (see below).\r\n- Pick 'Lean inward when cornering'  to get my H3R leaning outwards when cornering.  Go figure.\r\n- Set Motion scaling input to 5.0 and output to 17.0\r\nI'm using this effect to simulate cornering forces when taxiing on the ground. It also gives a great sideways kick when you touchdown on one wheel first.\r\n\r\nThis effect is controlled by the rudder pedals and there's a problem: when flying with S2R on things get very bumpy and feel wrong to me, yet I love the feeling on the ground.  What to do? I disable S2R when in the air.  \r\nHow do I do that?  Bind an effect toggle to my gear up/down lever. That can be done under Motion/Global Settings/Controls/Custom Controls/Per Effects/Sway to Roll/Toggle Activation. Both the gear up and gear down switches are bound to this toggle.\r\nSince this is a toggle and not a no/off binding I have to make sure the initial state of SimHub and my controller are correct.\r\nIf the flight/mission starts in the air the gear lever must be in the up position and S2R off (so I don't have bumpy yawing behaviour).\r\nIf it starts on the ground the gear lever must be down and S2R turned on.\r\nThat way after take off raising the gears turns off S2R and conversely when flying lowering the gears turns S2R on.\r\n\r\nHeave Effect\r\n- Increase Motion scaling input to 30.0 and output to 30.0 to get more bump when touching down.\r\n",
